{"problem": "iter_until_exc\n\nYields results from a function repeatedly until an exception is raised.\n\nConverts a call-until-exception interface to an iterator interface.\nLike ``iter(func, sentinel)``, but uses an exception instead of a sentinel\nto end the loop.\n\n    >>> l = [0, 1, 2]\n    >>> list(iter_until_exc(l.pop, IndexError))\n    [2, 1, 0]\n\nMultiple exceptions can be specified as a stopping condition:\n\n    >>> l = [1, 2, 3, '...', 4, 5, 6]\n    >>> list(iter_until_exc(lambda: 1 + l.pop(), (IndexError, TypeError)))\n    [7, 6, 5]\n    >>> list(iter_until_exc(lambda: 1 + l.pop(), (IndexError, TypeError)))\n    [4, 3, 2]\n    >>> list(iter_until_exc(lambda: 1 + l.pop(), (IndexError, TypeError)))\n    []", "resolution": "def iter_until_exc(func, exception, head=None):\n    \"\"\"Yields results from a function repeatedly until an exception is raised.\n\n    Converts a call-until-exception interface to an iterator interface.\n    Like ``iter(func, sentinel)``, but uses an exception instead of a sentinel\n    to end the loop.\n\n        >>> l = [0, 1, 2]\n        >>> list(iter_until_exc(l.pop, IndexError))\n        [2, 1, 0]\n\n    Multiple exceptions can be specified as a stopping condition:\n\n        >>> l = [1, 2, 3, '...', 4, 5, 6]\n        >>> list(iter_until_exc(lambda: 1 + l.pop(), (IndexError, TypeError)))\n        [7, 6, 5]\n        >>> list(iter_until_exc(lambda: 1 + l.pop(), (IndexError, TypeError)))\n        [4, 3, 2]\n        >>> list(iter_until_exc(lambda: 1 + l.pop(), (IndexError, TypeError)))\n        []\n\n    \"\"\"\n    with suppress(exception):\n        if head is not None:\n            yield head()\n        while True:\n            yield func()\n", "text": "iter_until_exc"}